\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Long did I toil, and knew no 
\par earthly rest;
\par Far did I rove, and found no
\par certain home;
\par At last I sought them in His
\par sheltering breast,
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par Who opes His arms, and bids 
\par the weary come:
\par With Him I found a home, 
\par a rest divine;
\par And I since then am His, and 
\par He is mine.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. The good I have is from His
\par stores supplied;
\par The ill is only what He deems
\par the best;
\par With Him as Friend I'm rich,
\par with nought beside,
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par And poor without Him, through
\par of all possest:
\par Changes may come- I take, or I
\par resign,
\par Content while I am His, while He
\par is mine.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Whate'er may change, in Him
\par no change is seen;
\par A glorious Sun, that wanes not, 
\par nor declines;
\par Above the clouds and storms 
\par He walks serene,
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par And on His people's inward
\par darkness shines:
\par All may depart- I fret not nor repine,
\par While I my Saviour's am, while
\par He is mine.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. While here, alas! I know but half
\par His love,
\par But half discern Him, and
\par but half adore;
\par But when I meet Him in 
\par the realms above,
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par I hope to love Him better, 
\par praise Him more,
\par And feel, and tell, amid
\par the choir divine,
\par How fully I am His, and He
\par is mine.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
\par }

